---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, ext } from "../data/site";

const updated = "8 October 2026";
const issues = `${site.repo}/issues`;

const h2 = "mt-14 text-2xl md:text-3xl";
const p = "mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/70";
const ul = "mt-4 max-w-2xl list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/70 marker:text-paper/30";
const link = "text-paper underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-paper";

// Data yang meninggalkan komputer pengguna. Disusun dari perilaku nyata Saya (main.js).
const flows = [
  {
    what: "Domain names you visit (DNS)",
    where: "Cloudflare, Google or Quad9 by default (DNS-over-HTTPS), or your system DNS",
    why: "To find the address of a website. Without it, nothing loads.",
    control: "Settings → DNS: pick Secure, Automatic or Off, and use any DNS provider you trust.",
  },
  {
    what: "What you type in the address bar",
    where: "Your selected search engine (DuckDuckGo by default), only while you are typing a search",
    why: "To show search suggestions. Things that look like web addresses are never sent.",
    control: "Turn suggestions off or make them local-only in config.json (suggestions.enabled / suggestions.remote).",
  },
  {
    what: "Your searches and the pages you open",
    where: "The search engine or website itself",
    why: "That is how browsing works. Those sites handle your data under their own policies.",
    control: "Choose another search engine (Ctrl+E), or block trackers with the built-in ad blocker.",
  },
  {
    what: "Ad blocker filter lists",
    where: "ublockorigin.github.io, easylist.to and raw.githubusercontent.com",
    why: "To download and refresh the rules that block ads and trackers. Only the lists are requested; none of your browsing is sent.",
    control: "Edit the list URLs or disable the blocker in config.json (adblock.lists / adblock.enabled).",
  },
];

const providers = [
  ["Cloudflare DNS", "https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"],
  ["Google (DNS and Google Search)", "https://policies.google.com/privacy"],
  ["Quad9 DNS", "https://quad9.net/privacy/policy/"],
  ["DuckDuckGo", "https://duckduckgo.com/privacy"],
  ["Brave Search", "https://search.brave.com/help/privacy-policy"],
  ["GitHub (downloads and filter lists)", "https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"],
];
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="What Saya stores on your computer, what leaves it, and who sees it.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pt-20">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-paper/50">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <p class={p}>
      {site.name} is a web browser that runs on your own computer. This page explains, in plain language, what it
      keeps on your device, what it sends over the internet, and what we (the maker, {site.owner}) can and cannot see.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>The short version</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>We do not run any servers that receive your browsing data. {site.name} has no account, no sign-in and no sync.</li>
      <li>{site.name} contains no analytics, no telemetry and no crash reporting that sends data to us.</li>
      <li>Your history, bookmarks, downloads list and settings stay on your computer.</li>
      <li>Like any browser, it has to talk to other services to work: DNS, your search engine and the sites you open. Those are listed below.</li>
      <li>We do not sell, rent or share personal data, because we do not have any.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      {site.owner} is the developer of {site.name}. Because the app collects nothing about you, there is no database
      of user data on our side. For any privacy question, open an issue at
      <a href={issues} class={link} {...ext(issues)}> GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>2. What {site.name} stores on your computer</h2>
    <p class={p}>These files live in the app's data folder inside your Windows user profile. They never leave your computer on their own.</p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li><strong class="font-normal text-paper">Browsing history</strong>: addresses and titles of pages, capped at 5,000 entries. The oldest entries are removed automatically.</li>
      <li><strong class="font-normal text-paper">Bookmarks</strong> and the list of recent <strong class="font-normal text-paper">downloads</strong> (names, addresses and file locations; the files themselves are in your Downloads folder).</li>
      <li><strong class="font-normal text-paper">Open tabs</strong>, window size and position, so your session can be restored next time.</li>
      <li><strong class="font-normal text-paper">Site permissions</strong> you granted or blocked (microphone, camera, location, clipboard), remembered per site.</li>
      <li><strong class="font-normal text-paper">Settings</strong>, plus your own ad-blocker rules and the sites where you paused the blocker.</li>
      <li><strong class="font-normal text-paper">Web data</strong> that websites save through the Chromium engine: cookies, local storage, IndexedDB and cache.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class={p}>
      {site.name} does not store passwords itself. Because this data is not encrypted by the app, anyone who can open your Windows user
      account can read it. Use a Windows password and disk encryption if others can access your computer.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>3. What leaves your computer</h2>
    <p class={p}>Everything below happens directly between your computer and the service named. It does not pass through us.</p>
    <ul class="mt-6 max-w-3xl divide-y divide-white/10 border-y border-white/10">
      {flows.map((f) => (
        <li class="grid gap-2 py-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl">{f.what}</h3>
          <p class="text-paper/70"><span class="text-paper/45">Goes to:</span> {f.where}</p>
          <p class="text-paper/70"><span class="text-paper/45">Why:</span> {f.why}</p>
          <p class="text-paper/70"><span class="text-paper/45">Your control:</span> {f.control}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>4. Browser identity</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      To keep websites working properly, {site.name} presents itself to sites as a Chromium-based browser on your
      operating system (it sends a Chrome-style User-Agent and matching client hints). Websites can therefore see
      your Windows version and that you use a Chromium-based browser. WebRTC is set to avoid revealing your local network address.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>5. Permissions</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      A website must ask before it can use your microphone, camera, location or clipboard contents, and your choice
      is remembered for that site only. Notifications are always blocked. You can review or reset a site's
      permissions from the site-info button in the address bar, or reset all of them from the menu.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>6. This website</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      This website is a static site. It does not use cookies, advertising or analytics scripts from us. Our hosting provider
      may keep standard server logs (such as IP address, browser type and time of request) for security and reliability.
      Downloads are served from GitHub, which has its own privacy statement.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>7. Third parties</h2>
    <p class={p}>These services receive data when you use the matching feature. Their own policies apply to what they do with it.</p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      {providers.map(([name, href]) => (
        <li><a href={href} class={link} {...ext(href)}>{name}</a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>8. Your controls</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>Clear history from the History page, and cache, cookies and site data from Settings.</li>
      <li>Turn off history, tab restore or remote suggestions in config.json (history.enabled, restoreTabs, suggestions.remote).</li>
      <li>Pause the ad blocker for any site from the site-info button or the right-click menu.</li>
      <li>Uninstalling {site.name} and deleting its data folder removes everything it stored.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Depending on where you live (for example under Indonesia's Personal Data Protection Law, the GDPR or the CCPA),
      you may have the right to access, correct, delete or object to the processing of your personal data. We do not
      hold personal data about {site.name} users, so there is nothing for us to retrieve or erase. If you believe we
      hold something about you, contact us and we will look into it.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>10. Children</h2>
    <p class={p}>{site.name} is a general-purpose browser and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone, including children.</p>

    <h2 class={h2}>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p class={p}>If the way {site.name} handles data changes, we will update this page and its date. Significant changes will also be noted in the release notes on GitHub.</p>

    <h2 class={h2}>12. Contact</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Questions or requests about privacy:
      <a href={issues} class={link} {...ext(issues)}> open an issue on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
